Dimitris Karapliafis and colleagues published RdRpCATCH in NAR Genomics and Bioinformatics on 27 June 2026.

RdRpCATCH consolidates eight published RNA-dependent RNA polymerase profile HMM databases into a single, user-friendly platform and enables scanning of (meta-)transcriptomic assemblies for RNA viruses. As described in the paper, the tool was developed as a community initiative following the 1st RdRp Summit, and it was presented as a keynote at the second RdRp Summit in Lisbon, May 2025.

RdRpCATCH: A unified resource for RNA virus discovery using viral RNA-dependent RNA polymerase profile Hidden Markov models. NAR Genomics and Bioinformatics 8(3), lqag076. [https://doi.org/10.1093/nargab/lqag076](https://doi.org/10.1093/nargab/lqag076)

Web server: [https://rdrpcatch.bioinformatics.nl](https://rdrpcatch.bioinformatics.nl)

Source: [https://github.com/dimitris-karapliafis/RdRpCATCH](https://github.com/dimitris-karapliafis/RdRpCATCH)
